Bob is cold (from the context).\n- Bob is furry (from the context).\n- Bob is smart (from the context).\n\nFrom the rules:.\n- Since Bob is smart, Bob must be green (because smart people are green).\n- Since Bob is furry, Bob must be big (because big people are cold, and we already know Bob is big and cold).\n- Since Bob is smart and furry, Bob must be big (reaffirming the previous point).\n\nNow, let\'s check the rule that if Gary is furry and Gary is not smart, then Gary is white. Gary is furry and not smart, but we don\'t know if Gary is white or not. However, this rule doesn\'t directly apply to Bob.\n\nNext, let\'s check the rule that if Bob is not green and Bob is not white, then Bob is furry. Since Bob is smart and therefore green, this rule does not apply to Bob.\n\nFinally, let\'s check the rule that if someone is white and not cold, then they are not blue. Since Bob is cold, this rule does not apply to Bob.\n\nGiven all the information and rules, we can conclude that Bob is not white because:.\n- Bob is smart, so he is green.\n- Bob is furry, so he is big.\n- Bob is not white because if Bob were white, he would have to be cold (since all cold people are not blue, and Bob is cold). Therefore, my final option is: ']]
