d.**.\n    - This tells us that Anne, being young, is kind.\n\nFrom the above analysis, we can conclude:.\n- Harry is big and kind.\n- Since all kind people are rough, Harry must be rough.\n- Since all young people are kind, Anne is young and kind.\n- Since all young people are kind, Anne is also kind.\n- Since Anne is cold and rough, and if Anne is cold and rough then Anne is smart, Anne is smart.\n- Since Harry is kind and Harry is rough, Harry is smart.\n\nHowever, the question specifically asks about Harry being cold. From the information provided, we know that Harry is big and kind, but we do not have any direct information about Harry\'s coldness.\n\nTherefore, based on the given information, the statement "Harry is cold" is **unknown**. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
