n6. **If someone is young then they are kind.**.\n   - From the context: "If Anne is young then Anne is kind.".\n   - Since Dave is young, it follows that Dave is kind.\n\n7. **All kind, cold people are nice.**.\n   - From the context: "All kind, cold people are nice.".\n   - Since Dave is cold and kind, he would be nice according to this rule.\n\nGiven the above analysis, we can conclude that Dave is both cold and kind, which means he is nice. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
