 the dog.\n   - If something sees the bear and the bear is young, then the bear is rough.\n   - If something chases the bear and the bear is young, then the bear chases the dog.\n\n3. **Tiger and Bear Relationships:**.\n   - The tiger sees the cow.\n   - The dog does not like the tiger.\n   - The tiger is not big.\n   - The tiger does not see the bear.\n   - The tiger chases the bear (this is what we need to determine).\n\n### Analysis of the Statement "The tiger chases the bear":.\n\n- From the context, we know that the tiger sees the cow.\n- The statement "If something chases the dog and it is cold, then it is young" does not directly apply to the tiger chasing the bear.\n- The statement "If the bear likes the cow, then the cow chases the dog" does not directly apply to the tiger chasing the bear.\n- The statement "If something chases the bear and the bear is young, then the bear chases the dog" does not directly apply to the tiger chasing the bear.\n- The statement "The tiger sees the cow" does not provide information about the tiger chasing the bear.\n\nGiven the information, there is no direct statement that explicitly says the tiger chases the bear. The only information we have is that the tiger sees the cow, but this does not imply that the tiger chases the bear.\n\n### Conclusion:. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
