text).\n   - If the tiger needs the rabbit, then the tiger visits the rabbit (from the context).\n   - If the tiger visits the rabbit, then the tiger is not green (from the context).\n   - If the tiger visits the rabbit, then the tiger visits the bald eagle (from the context).\n\n3. **Conclusion:**\n   - Since the rabbit needs the bald eagle, and the rabbit chases the tiger (because the rabbit needs the bald eagle and the tiger needs the rabbit), the tiger visits the rabbit.\n   - Therefore, the tiger visits the bald eagle.\n\nGiven that the rabbit chases the tiger, and the tiger visits the bald eagle, the rabbit must visit the bald eagle as well.\n\n### Final Answer:\nThe statement "The rabbit does not visit the bald eagle" is **False**.\n\n**Option B: False**. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
