 not apply to her.\n\n7. **If someone is white then they are blue.**.\n   - This statement is not directly relevant to Fiona, as she is not white.\n\n8. **If Charlie is quiet then Charlie is white.**.\n   - Charlie is quiet, but we don\'t know if he is white or not. This statement does not directly apply to Fiona.\n\n### Conclusion:.\n- Fiona is explicitly stated to be kind.\n- There is no information that contradicts or makes the statement "Fiona is not kind" true.\n\nTherefore, the statement "Fiona is not kind" is **false**. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
