e tiger and the tiger visits the lion, then it sees the bald eagle.\n19. If the lion sees the bald eagle, then the bald eagle visits the tiger.\n20. If something is young, then it visits the lion.\n\n### Analysis:.\n- From the given information, we know that the cat chases the lion (point 3).\n- The statement we need to verify is "The bald eagle chases the cat.".\n- According to point 15, if something sees the lion and it sees the bald eagle, then it chases the cat.\n- We need to check if there is any information that satisfies the condition of "seeing the lion and seeing the bald eagle" for the bald eagle.\n\n### Checking the Conditions:.\n- The bald eagle is green and red (points 1 and 2).\n- The lion is red (point 8).\n- The bald eagle sees the lion (point 9).\n- The lion sees the bald eagle (point 9).\n\nSince the bald eagle sees the lion and the lion sees the bald eagle, according to point 15, the bald eagle should chase the cat.\n\n### Conclusion:.\nThe bald eagle chases the cat based on the given information and the logical conditions provided.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
