t mentioned as being rough, so this statement does not apply to Fiona.\n\n- **"Cold, furry things are white."**.\n  - Anne is cold and furry, but we don\'t know if she is white.\n\n- **"All rough, nice things are young."**.\n  - Bob is not mentioned as being nice, so this statement does not apply to Bob.\n\n- **"If something is white and furry then it is smart."**.\n  - Anne is white and furry, but we don\'t know if she is smart.\n\nFrom the given information, we can see that:.\n- Anne is cold and furry, but we don\'t have any information about her being young.\n- Erin is young and cold, but we don\'t have any information about Anne being young.\n\nSince Anne is not explicitly mentioned as being young, and we have no information that directly or indirectly confirms or denies her being young, the statement "Anne is young" is unknown based on the given information.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
